# React: Effect-Last (Avoid `useEffect`)

Default rule: do **not** add `useEffect` for normal app logic.

`useEffect` is allowed only when synchronizing with an external system (for example: browser APIs, subscriptions, timers, analytics, third-party widgets, websocket lifecycle).

## Rules

- **No derived state in effects**: If a value can be computed from props/state, compute it during render (or `useMemo` if needed).
- **No event logic in effects**: Put user-triggered behavior in event handlers, not in effect chains.
- **No fetch-on-render effects by default**: Prefer framework/data abstractions (Server Components, route loaders/actions, TanStack Query, SWR, etc.) over manual fetch effects.
- **No direct `useEffect` imports in feature code**: Use existing abstractions/hooks first.
- **Mount-only sync is rare**: If a one-time mount sync is truly required, use a dedicated wrapper hook such as `useMountEffect`.

## Allowed Use Cases

- Subscribing/unsubscribing to external event sources
- Integrating imperative third-party libraries
- Managing timers tied to component lifecycle
- Syncing with browser APIs that are not render-safe

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — derived state via effect
const [fullName, setFullName] = useState("");
useEffect(() => {
  setFullName(`${user.firstName} ${user.lastName}`);
}, [user.firstName, user.lastName]);

// ✅ GOOD — derive during render
const fullName = `${user.firstName} ${user.lastName}`;
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — event flow through effect
useEffect(() => {
  if (isSubmitted) {
    toast.success("Lagt til");
  }
}, [isSubmitted]);

// ✅ GOOD — keep in handler
async function onSubmit() {
  await save();
  toast.success("Lagt til");
}
```

```tsx
// Rare escape hatch for true mount-only external sync
export function useMountEffect(effect: () => void | (() => void)) {
  useEffect(effect, []);
}
```
